{"name":"Air of Mint","hex":"#d8f2ee","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"air","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Airoran."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance constituting Earth's atmosphere: a gaseous mixture of nitrogen, oxygen, and various trace gases.","The substance of the atmosphere seen as an agency of freshness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/air"},{"term":"mint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building or institution where money (originally, only coins) is produced under government licence.","A vast sum of money;  a large amount of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reproduce (coins), usually en masse, under licence.","To invent; to forge; to fabricate; to fashion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mint (facility)","blocks":[{"text":"A mint is an industrial facility which manufactures coins that can be used as currency."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/United_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg/330px-United_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mint_(facility)","wikidata":"Q464780"},{"title":"Atmosphere of Earth","blocks":[{"text":"The atmosphere of Earth consists of a layer of mixed gas that is retained by gravity, surrounding the Earth's surface. It contains variable quantities of suspended aerosols and particulates that create weather features such as clouds and hazes. The atmosphere serves as a protective buffer between the Earth's surface and outer space. It shields the surface from most meteoroids and ultraviolet solar radiation, reduces diurnal temperature variation – the temperature extremes between day and night – and keeps it warm through heat retention via the greenhouse effect. The atmosphere redistributes heat and moisture among different regions via air currents, and provides the chemical and climate conditions that allow life to exist and evolve on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg/330px-Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atmosphere_of_Earth","wikidata":"Q3230"},{"title":"Spring green","blocks":[{"text":"Spring green is a color that was traditionally considered to be on the yellow side of green, but in modern computer systems based on the RGB color model is halfway between cyan and green on the color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_green","wikidata":"Q373787"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/United_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg/500px-United_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/United_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg/1280px-United_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/United_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg/500px-United_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"United States Mint, Philadelphia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUnited_States_Mint%2C_Philadelphia%2C_Aug_2019.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Mold_for_making_banliang_coins.jpg/500px-Mold_for_making_banliang_coins.jpg?utm_source=